Use io.

Define function reverse_integer taking value as a whole number returning a whole number:
    Let sign start at 1.
    Let magnitude be value.
    If magnitude is negative:
        Set sign to -1.
        Set magnitude to 0 - magnitude.
    Let reversed start at 0.
    Repeat while magnitude > 0:
        Let digit be magnitude modulo 10.
        Set reversed to reversed * 10 + digit.
        Divide magnitude by 10.
    If reversed is more than 2147483647:
        Give back 0.
    Give back reversed * sign.
Done.

Say reverse_integer(123).
Say reverse_integer(-123).
Say reverse_integer(120).
Say reverse_integer(1534236469).
Return 0.
